docs/service-contract.md:180:Claims a statement does not select, including `sub`, repository IDs, owner IDs, and actor metadata, do not affect authorization. A GitHub Actions token that fails its OIDC ID Token Profile, including an invalid `azp` claim, remains an invalid subject token and returns `400 {"error":"invalid_request"}`. Repository identity remains name-based; a repository deleted and recreated with the same owner/name can continue to match when the GitHub App installation still grants sufficient permissions.
